  "literature_notes": "CD20 (MS4A1) has two extracellular spans: ECL1 (residues 79\u201384, only 6 aa) and ECL2 (residues 142\u2013188, 47 aa). Both termini are intracellular (N-term 1\u201356, C-term 210\u2013297). L1 reports a C-terminal DYKDHDID (FLAG-like) tag on bovine and feline CD20 full-length constructs, confirmed at the cell surface by flow cytometry; however, the CD20 C-terminus is intracellular (residues 210\u2013297 per the authoritative topology landmarks), so this tag faces the cytoplasm and cannot serve as an extracellular surface tag \u2014 it is recorded in other_positions. L2 describes flow-cytometric analysis of canine CD20 mutants M1\u2013M5 using anti-CD20 antibody 4E1-7-B_f; this is an antibody-binding/epitope-mapping study on substitution mutants, not a tag-insertion experiment, and no residue number for a tag junction is given. It therefore does not qualify under the evidence rules. No ledger line grounds an extracellular tag insertion for MS4A1.",
